    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Sleepless driving is an innovative technology that can save lives. We believe that it is not only practical to implement our technology in cars, but a necessary safety feature comparable to the seat belt. Driving is already a dangerous enough activity while fully focused and aware of your surroundings, so our argument is why shouldn’t cars be equipped with technology that can actively monitor whether or not the driver is fully awake and conscious.  The technology is available and can be implemented in cars by putting sensors on the steering wheel that can monitor heart rate, stress, brain waves, and the activity in the cortex.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
